    "q-143273": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143273",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{49}∼N(-7,{14}^{2})$ is a random sample of size $n=49$ from a normal population, what is the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}?$",
      "worked_solution": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nn=49,\\,\\mu =-7,\\,\\sigma =14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(-7,\\frac{{14}^{2}}{49}) \\\\  & ∼N(-7,4).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
